course: dictionary
lesson: 14710
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The clues in the sentence show you which meaning the writer means. «Processed» is one of these words.
explain: «The factory processed the apples into juice.» Here processed means changed by a machine. Test it: "The factory changed the apples into juice" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «Your form has been processed, so the office will write back soon.» Here processed means dealt with officially, the way offices handle forms and requests. The clue is the office and the letter that will follow.
explain: Some grown-ups use «processed» about farm animals that are killed for meat. This is jargon, the special words used in one trade, and it is a euphemism, a soft word used in place of a harder one. Ask yourself: does this word make something sound cleaner than it really is?
fact: Processed means changed by a machine or factory, or dealt with officially.
fact: A word can have several meanings, so always check the clues in the sentence.
fact: A euphemism is a soft, polite word used in place of a harsh one.
fact: In the meat industry, «processed» can be a euphemism: it sounds clean but hides that animals were killed.
fact: Jargon means special words used by people who work in one job or field.
exercise: «The factory processed the corn into cereal.» What does processed mean here? | Sung loudly | Lost in the post | Cooked in a pan at home | *Changed by a machine
exercise: «My form has been processed, so the office will write back soon.» What does processed mean? | Made in a kitchen | Broken into small pieces | Washed clean | *Dealt with officially
exercise: «The report said the farm processed 300 pigs each week.» Why might the writer choose processed? | It means the farm sold them as pets | *It is a soft, clean word that hides the harsh truth that animals were killed for meat | It means the pigs were moved to a new farm | It means the pigs were fed and kept warm
test: «The machine processed the cocoa beans into chocolate.» What does processed mean? | Stirred with a spoon | *Changed by a machine | Thrown away | Hidden in a box
test: «Your library card application has been processed.» What does this tell you? | The card is too big to carry | The librarian is ill | *It has been dealt with officially | The card was lost in the post
exam: Some people say «processed» when they mean animals were killed for meat. What kind of word is this? | *A euphemism, a soft word that hides a harsh truth | A kind of official form | Slang for a sweet | A type of machine
